From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: 994 - island prevention must check the uplink reaches the controller

Island prevention exists to stop a node without an uplink from serving anyone:
on backhaul loss it takes the BSSes down, ignores connect attempts and
disassociates STAs. It bails out early whenever the backhaul looks regained --
and that test is agent_has_active_backhaul(), which only asks whether some bSTA
is associated:

  bool agent_has_active_backhaul(struct agent *a)
  {
  	return (agent_is_bsta_connected(a) || agent_is_backhaul_type_eth());
  }

Nothing there asks whether the association leads anywhere. Two agents that pick
each other's backhaul BSS -- trivial once both advertise the same backhaul SSID,
because a bSTA selects on SSID and nothing else -- each see a connected bSTA,
each conclude the backhaul is fine, and neither takes its backhaul BSS down.
The pair then holds each other up with no path to the controller. Observed on
hardware 2026-07-26: 8g associated to x8, x8 to 8g, both with a default route
they could not use, topology_link=0, and the state was stable rather than
oscillating. A cold power cycle reproduced it, because both agents boot at once
and have their backhaul BSSes up before either reaches the controller.

Add agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr() and use it at the three island-prevention
sites that mean "the backhaul came back". active_cntlr is the missing half of
the question: it is set on every CMDU received from the controller and cleared
only after max_misstime without one, so a brief controller outage does not trip
this, while a mutual lock -- where neither side ever hears from the controller --
does. Wired backhaul keeps returning true unconditionally.

agent_has_active_backhaul() itself is left alone: it has ten callers with other
meanings, and the fault is specific to the "regained" test.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/backhaul.c
+++ b/src/backhaul.c
@@ -800,6 +800,24 @@
 	return (agent_is_bsta_connected(a) || agent_is_backhaul_type_eth());
 }
 
+/* 994: an uplink only counts as regained if it actually leads to the
+ * controller. Two agents that associate to each other's backhaul BSS both see
+ * a connected bSTA, so both bail out of island prevention, neither takes its
+ * backhaul BSS down, and the pair deadlocks with no path to the controller --
+ * observed on hardware. active_cntlr is the missing half of the question: it
+ * is set on every CMDU received from the controller (agent_map.c) and only
+ * cleared after max_misstime without one, so a brief controller outage does
+ * not trip this while a mutual lock, where neither side ever hears from the
+ * controller, does.
+ */
+bool agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr(struct agent *a)
+{
+	if (agent_is_backhaul_type_eth())
+		return true;
+
+	return agent_is_bsta_connected(a) && a->active_cntlr;
+}
+
 char *agent_get_backhaul_ifname(struct agent *a, char *ifname)
 {
 	struct blob_buf bk = { 0 };
--- a/src/backhaul.h
+++ b/src/backhaul.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 bool agent_is_bsta_onboarded(struct agent *a);
 bool agent_is_backhaul_type_eth(void);
 bool agent_has_active_backhaul(struct agent *a);
+bool agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr(struct agent *a);
 char *agent_get_backhaul_ifname(struct agent *a, char *ifname);
 void agent_trigger_bsta_sync(atimer_t *t);
 void agent_update_active_uplink(struct agent *a, struct netif_bk *bk);
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -2125,7 +2125,7 @@
 	trace("%s: --->\n", __func__);
 	struct wifi_radio_element *re = NULL;
 
-	if (agent_has_active_backhaul(a))
+	if (agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr(a))
 		/* backhaul regained, don't send BTM */
 		return;
 
@@ -2171,7 +2171,7 @@
 	struct agent *a = container_of(t, struct agent, fh_disable_timer);
 	struct wifi_radio_element *re = NULL;
 
-	if (agent_has_active_backhaul(a))
+	if (agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr(a))
 		/* backhaul regained, don't disable FHs */
 		return;
 
@@ -2198,7 +2198,7 @@
 	struct agent *a = container_of(t, struct agent, sta_disconnect_timer);
 	struct wifi_radio_element *re = NULL;
 
-	if (agent_has_active_backhaul(a))
+	if (agent_backhaul_reaches_cntlr(a))
 		/* backhaul regained, don't disconnect STAs */
 		return;
 
